    "notes": "Inspected all 48 final current source, shared-material, medium-fi, native-site and failed-load views in this continuous round. The main red hall has a real round arched passage, pale arch trim, open lattice windows, curved green roof and slender red/white tiered pagoda at its south side. Separate ranges rise on hillside terraces around open inner courts. The northern granite gateway has an open red-jamb passage, paired curling ridge forms and central pearl, two red lanterns, stairs, balustrades and simplified seated guardian lions. The rear northern pavilion has an open post-supported porch. Roof subdivisions, terrace engineering and internal allocation are approximate; no exact hidden-room inventory."
  },
